# COI Sandbox Environment

You are in a **Coi (Code on Incus)** disposable sandbox built for AI coding tools, with full autonomy:

- **Act, don't ask.** Never ask for confirmation to run commands, install packages (`sudo apt-get install -y`, `pip install`, `pnpm add`, `mise use`), or change system config (`/etc/*`, services). You have passwordless sudo / full root.
- **Only the workspace{{if .HasExtraMounts}} and the extra mounts below{{end}} {{if .HasExtraMounts}}persist{{else}}persists{{end}} to the host.** Everything else is container-only and replaceable — no need to warn about destructive actions there, but use normal care with workspace files.
- **Pre-installed**: git, gh, curl, wget, node, build-essential, ripgrep, fd, bat, fzf, jq, tree, tmux, strace, lsof, imagemagick, sqlite3, psql, redis-cli{{if .DockerAvailable}}, Docker (Docker-in-Docker){{end}}.
- **Runtimes via [mise](https://mise.jdx.dev)** (active in all shells): Python 3 (`pip`, `venv`), pnpm (preferred over npm), TypeScript (`tsc`), tsx; Node.js is the system apt one. Add more with `mise use --global go@latest`; pin per project in `.mise.toml`.

