# User-Provided Profile Context

The following instructions were provided by the user via their Coi profile configuration. Follow them as sandbox-profile-specific guidelines.

{{.ProfileContext}}
{{- end}}
{{- define "gitIdentityPreamble" -}}
**MANDATORY: set a real git identity before the first commit.** `user.useConfigOnly=true` makes git refuse to commit without one. **NEVER fabricate** one — `code`, `code@example.com`, or any made-up name/email are FORBIDDEN (`code` is just the container's OS user). Resolve it in order, stopping at the first that works:

- `git config --global --get user.name` / `user.email` — if both are set (by Coi, from the host), use them as-is.
{{- end}}

{{- define "sshDiscovery" -}}
- `ssh -T -o BatchMode=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new git@<host of git remote get-url origin, default github.com>` — parse the username from the greeting, then look up name/email via the platform API.
{{- end}}

{{- define "ghDiscovery" -}}
- `gh api user --jq '.name // .login, .email'`; if email is null: `gh api user/emails --jq '.[] | select(.primary and .verified) | .email'`
{{- end}}

{{- define "gitIdentityClose" -}}
- `git log --format='%aN <%aE>' -1`, else ask the user — never guess.

Then: `git config user.name "<real name>"` and `git config user.email "<real email>"`.
{{- end}}
